{"verdict": "supported",
  "answer": "The evidence directly links RANK–RANKL signalling to the development of Aire-expressing medullary thymic epithelial cells (mTECs). RANK signalling was essential during embryogenesis, and RANKL signals from CD4+3− inducer cells promote maturation of RANK-expressing CD80−Aire− mTEC progenitors into CD80+Aire+ mTECs, with ligation of RANK on fetal thymic stroma inducing mTEC development via TRAF6, NIK and IKKβ. RANK-deficient thymic stroma transplanted into immunodeficient hosts induced autoimmunity, further tying the pathway to Aire+ mTEC generation and self-tolerance.",
  "evidence_used": ["2734421", "301838", "3952288"]}
